multiplexing  serial  communications  interface For 4‐port BB1004
boards: For 8‐port BB1008 boards: For 16‐port BB2016 boards: (The
BB2016 is functionally equivalent to two BB1008  boards,  and  is
configured  as  such.)   The driver provides support for BOCA Re‐
search BB1004, BB1008 and BB2016 boards that  multiplex  together
up to four, eight or sixteen communications interfaces.  Each de‐
vice  is  the  master device for up to eight devices.  The kernel
configuration specifies these devices as slave devices of the de‐
vice, as shown in the synopsis.  The slave ID given for each  de‐
vice  determines which bit in the interrupt multiplexing register
is tested to find interrupts for that device.  The  specification
for the device is used to compute the base addresses for the sub‐
devices  and  the  port  for the interrupt multiplexing register.
The driver was written by Charles Hannum, based on the driver and
source code from David Muir Sharnoff.  David wishes  to  acknowl‐
edge the assistance of Jason Venner in determining how to use the
BOCA boards.
